cal Error** \u2013 many of the listed points lie outside \\(T_k\\) (their sums exceed \\(2m+2\\)), and the count \\(m+1\\) is incorrect for several \\(j\\).\n\n* **Location:** \u201cTake any \\((a,b)\\in T_k\\). Set \\(j:=b-a\\). \u2026 Substituting \\(j=b-a\\) into (8) gives \\(b=-2a+2m+2+(b-a)\\), which is precisely the equation of the line \\(L_{\\,b-a}\\). Hence \\((a,b)\\) lies on \\(L_{\\,b-a}\\).\u201d  \n  **Issue:** **Critical Error** \u2013 the algebraic manipulation is wrong; after substitution one obtains \\(0=-3a+2m+2\\), which is not satisfied by a generic \\((a,b)\\). Thus the claimed covering fails.\n\n* **Location:** Final statement \u2013 \u201cHence the admissible values of \\(k\\) are exactly \\(k=0\\) or \\(k\\) odd, \\(1\\le k\\le n\\).\u201d  \n  **Issue:** **Critical Error** \u2013 the existence part for odd\u202f\\(k\\) rests on the faulty construction above; without a valid covering the conclusion is unsupported.\n\n---\n\n## Detailed Verification Log\n\n### 1. Definition of the point set \\(S_n\\)\n\n> \u201cLet  \n> \\[\n> S_n=\\{(a,b)\\in\\mathbb Z_{>0}^2\\mid a+b\\le n+1\\},\n> \\qquad |S_n|=\\frac{n(n+1)}2 .\n> \\]\u201d\n\n*Correct.*  The set consists of all lattice points with positive coordinates whose sum does not exceed \\(n+1\\); the count is the triangular number \\(\\frac{n(n+1)}2\\). No issue.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Reduction to a triangular lattice\n\n> \u201cFix an integer \\(k\\) with \\(0\\le k\\le n\\).  \n> Place the \\(n-k\\) vertical lines  \n> \\[\n> V_i:\\;x=i\\qquad(i=1,2,\\dots ,n-k).\n> \\tag{1}\n> \\]  \n> \u2026  \n> The points that remain uncovered are precisely  \n> \\[\n> T_k=\\{(a,b)\\in\\mathbb Z_{>0}^2\\mid a+b\\le k+1\\},\n> \\tag{2}\n> \\]\u201d\n\n**Analysis.**  \nThe vertical lines cover all points of \\(S_n\\) whose first coordinate \\(a\\) satisfies \\(1\\le a\\le n-k\\).  \nThe *remaining* points satisfy \\(a\\ge n-k+1\\) and \\(a+b\\le n+1\\).  \nIf we set \\(a' = a-(n-k)\\) (so \\(a'\\ge1\\)), the condi